**/dumps
**/target
*~
*.swp
.env
galos_db/backups/*
.galos_index
# An index written under another name, which is what `--index DIR`
# invites, and the lock a run takes beside whichever it writes. A built
# directory is derived and large, and a lock is one process's claim on it;
# none of it belongs here. Named one at a time on purpose: a glob over
# `*.lock` would take `Cargo.lock` with it.
.galos_index.lock
.galos_journal_index
.galos_journal_index.lock
/my_index
/my_index.lock
# Where a build under test is put when several are wanted at once:
# `--index .index/NAME`, each with its own lock and resume point beside
# it.
/.index
# A resume point is named after the directory it resumes, so an index
# written anywhere but the default carries its own. The bare
# `.galos_checkpoint` is what runs older than that wrote.
*.checkpoint
*.checkpoint.pending
.galos_checkpoint*
# Catalogs are downloaded and handed to `galos-catalog` as a path, not
# vendored. `bright.csv` is the exception: it is `include_str!`d as the
# fixture the consistency and comparison tests read, so it stays.
galos_catalog/data/*
!galos_catalog/data/bright.csv

# Working notes and design write-ups, gathered in one place and kept out of
# the repository. Listed rather than left merely untracked because a wide
# `git add` has swept them in before. `ARCHITECTURE.md` is the exception:
# it describes the code that exists rather than work that does not, and the
# top-level README points a reader at it.
/doc/*
!/doc/ARCHITECTURE.md

# Whatever is open, in whatever shape it is in. Not under `doc/`: a TODO is
# a scratch file that wants to be in the way, and one collapsed file today
# is several again the moment a new thread starts.
/TODO.md
TODO-*

# `galos-sky`'s default output, and a sample figure file handed to
# `--figures`. Both are run artifacts rather than sources.
/sky.png
galos_sky/figures.fab
